The work on karr #18/#19/#23 was held to read-only probes and the daemon had no containers, so three things went into t/containers_endpoints.t unmeasured:

  - t/fixtures/containers_archive.tar is a real ustar archive built with GNU
    tar, shaped like what GET /containers/{id}/archive?path=/etc/hostname
    returns. It is not a daemon capture. Every other tar fixture in t/ is.
  - the attach subtests reuse t/fixtures/containers_logs_multiplexed.bin,
    on the (documented, not measured here) ground that the one-way attach
    stream is byte-identical to the logs stream.
  - the X-Docker-Container-Path-Stat payload is constructed in the test from
    the key names the Docker Engine API documents (name, size, mode, mtime,
    linkTarget). Podman's spelling of them is unverified, and mode is claimed
    to be Go os.FileMode bits rather than a POSIX mode word.

With API_DOCKER_TEST_WRITE=1 against the Podman socket, capture the three for
real and replace the constructed ones. The live subtest at the bottom of
t/containers_endpoints.t already reads and notes the header keys off any
container that happens to exist -- it skipped on the run that added it.
